IFC Canvas modification to mapbox/earcut.hpp (https://github.com/mapbox/earcut.hpp).
Applies to earcut.hpp upstream commit 4811a2b69b91f6127a75e780de6e2113609ddabb,
the revision that web-ifc f26c4beef0a668ebdb180d2b95a94097a1e21cef (tag 0.77)
fetches with CMake FetchContent. Apply it with `git apply` inside the fetched
earcut source directory (<cmake build dir>/_deps/earcut-src).
How it was made: IFC Canvas 0.96.4 to 1.1.24 made this change at build time
with four `perl -0777 -pi` substitutions on include/mapbox/earcut.hpp, not
with a patch file (the four lines are quoted in README.md next to this file).
This diff was generated by running those four substitutions unchanged on
earcut.hpp at the commit above and diffing the result against the unmodified
file; applying it reproduces their output byte for byte (git blob
e87540bd4c5376d6d54b3b1229684df996a4314b).
License: ISC, the license of earcut.hpp itself (Copyright (c) 2015, Mapbox);
see LICENSE-earcut-ISC.txt next to this file.
Changes:
  - three cooperative-cancellation checks that call web-ifc's
    webifc::geometry::CheckCancellation() (declared in
    src/cpp/web-ifc/geometry/IfcCancellation.h of this fork): at the entry of
    earcutLinked(), and every 1024 iterations of the earcutLinked() ear-slicing
    loop and of the cureLocalIntersections() walk, so a per-element time
    budget can abort a triangulation that does not terminate.

